{"name":"Steamboat Geyser","hex":"#d2ccb4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"steamboat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A boat or vessel propelled by steam power.","Hot pot (Chinese dish)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To travel by steamboat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steamboat"},{"term":"geyser","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A boiling natural spring which throws forth jets of water, mud, etc., at frequent intervals, driven upwards by the expansive power of steam.","A momentary vertical jet or fountain of fluid driven upwards by a violent force."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To (cause to) rush or burst upward like water from a geyser."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/geyser"}],"entries":[{"title":"Steamboat Geyser","blocks":[{"text":"Steamboat Geyser, in Yellowstone National Park's Norris Geyser Basin, is the world's tallest active geyser. Steamboat Geyser has two vents, northern and southern, approximately 20 feet (6.1 m) apart. The north vent is responsible for the tallest water columns; the south vent's water columns are shorter."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Steamboatgeyser1.jpg/330px-Steamboatgeyser1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steamboat_Geyser","wikidata":"Q1438568"},{"title":"Steamboat","blocks":[{"text":"A steamboat is a boat that is propelled primarily by steam power, typically driving propellers or paddlewheels. The term steamboat is used to refer to small steam-powered vessels working on lakes, rivers, and in short-sea shipping. The development of the steamboat led to the larger steamship, which is a seaworthy and often ocean-going ship."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/%22Look_out%22_%28Transport_Steamer%29_on_Tennessee_River_-_NARA_-_5289791_restored.jpg/330px-%22Look_out%22_%28Transport_Steamer%29_on_Tennessee_River_-_NARA_-_5289791_restored.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steamboat","wikidata":"Q178193"},{"title":"Geyser","blocks":[{"text":"A geyser is a spring with an intermittent water discharge ejected turbulently and accompanied by steam. The formation of geysers is fairly rare and is caused by particular hydrogeological conditions that exist only in a few places on Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Yellowstone_National_Park_%28WY%2C_USA%29%2C_Old_Faithful_Geyser_--_2022_--_2599.jpg/330px-Yellowstone_National_Park_%28WY%2C_USA%29%2C_Old_Faithful_Geyser_--_2022_--_2599.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geyser","wikidata":"Q83471"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/NorrisGeyserBasinSteamboat.JPG/500px-NorrisGeyserBasinSteamboat.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/NorrisGeyserBasinSteamboat.JPG/500px-NorrisGeyserBasinSteamboat.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANorrisGeyserBasinSteamboat.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/B_MG_2505A.jpg/500px-B_MG_2505A.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/B_MG_2505A.jpg/1280px-B_MG_2505A.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/B_MG_2505A.jpg/500px-B_MG_2505A.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Steamboat Geyser, major eruption, August 4, 2018","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AB_MG_2505A.jpg"},{"src